  "title": "Human es-fMRI Resource: Concurrent deep-brain stimulation and whole-brain functional MRI",
  "description": "This dataset contains concurrent electrical stimulation and functional MRI (es-fMRI) recordings from 26 patients with medically refractory epilepsy who had intracranial electrodes implanted in cortical and subcortical sites. Selected electrode contacts were stimulated in a block design while whole-brain BOLD activity was recorded. The resource includes pre-operative and post-operative sessions, structural scans, resting-state scans, field maps, stimulation coordinates and parameters, and fMRIPrep and FreeSurfer derivatives.",
  "methods_description": "Patients underwent es-fMRI after surgical implantation of intracranial electrodes. One or more contacts were stimulated in a block design during BOLD-fMRI acquisition. Pre-operative sessions included T1, T2 and resting-state scans. Post-operative sessions included es-fMRI runs, field maps, stimulation electrode coordinates and stimulation parameters. Preprocessing used fMRIPrep and FreeSurfer.",
